# A CANDIDATE: A STREAM THAT FAILS AFTER ITS FIRST CHUNK FAILS (the
# architecture session, 2026-11-25: "THE STREAM FIX IS A DEFECT OF TODAY'S
# ENGINE - a mid-answer error ends a chat answer as complete and shorter, on
# the 9B and the 35B, now ... put it into the series that is built next
# rather than behind parking: 'fix it after' is not an option for a truncated
# answer delivered as whole"). aa88ab5c356a's series (engine-lang), line for
# line, then:
#   0025  LocalAI's backend: an error AFTER the first chunk of a stream ends
#         the stream with that error, where it was written as an empty reply
#         and the call returned OK (localai-bugs.md B21).
#   0026  a TEST switch, so that the card can show it: GGML_SYCL_GRAPH_REFUSE=N
#         with GGML_SYCL_GRAPH_REFUSE_ARM=<file> - once the file exists the
#         next N graphs are abandoned as after a refused pool commit. Off
#         unless a model's env sets both; it computes nothing.
#   SERIES_FILE=deploy/localai/patches/staged/engine-stream.series \
#     sh deploy/localai/llama-cpp/build.sh sycl_f16 <out dir>      # the live INTEL_STACK
# ONE BUILD, ONE GATING for the paging default (0021), the language tag (0022)
# and the stream: it stands in d658549772ca's and aa88ab5c356a's place if
# neither is gated yet. Its own row, on a COPY of a chat model:
#   python3 -I tools/measure/stream_fails_test.py --addr ADDR --arm <file>
